            <ArticleTitle>Development of coronary aneurysm after cutting balloon angioplasty: assessment by intracoronary ultrasound.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>449-52</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report the case of a coronary aneurysm observed 6 mo after cutting balloon angioplasty complicated by a mild perforation. Intravascular ultrasound allowed characterization of the malformation as a true aneurysm. The clinical course was uneventful.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
